DAW Pro local patch 0003 against signalsmith-stretch v1.3.2 (57b93f4e9206a089a45387eaa39bdc9f310d3308) + patches 0001, 0002

Exact previous hop: re-analyse the previous spectrum whenever the input
interval differs from the synthesis hop H at all.

Upstream kept the previous block's spectrum when |interval - H| <= 1 ("give or
take 1 sample"), but the `rot` pass (and patch 0002's peak position) turn it
by exactly H. On a hop whose interval is H-1 or H+1 the output therefore
advanced at omega*(H+-1)/H: up to 1.2 c (48 kHz) / 1.3 c (44.1 kHz) on those
hops, a measured mean of up to 0.93 c on a pure time-stretch, at 0 st too.
Such hops occur only at ratios within about 2.6/H of 1 (measured: 2.58/H in
the 4096-frame constant loop, 2.00/H in the per-hop curve loop), e.g. a
64-beat clip stretched by one 1/16 step (1.0009766). Elsewhere upstream
already re-analysed every hop, so bytes there are unchanged.

Cost: one extra analysis FFT per channel on those hops only (+8.6 % at ratio
1.0005, still below the cost of any ratio outside the window).
THIS PATCH CHANGES 0-st BYTES at near-unity ratios: the render cache must
re-key them (StretchRenderCache, `pv:` predicate).

Conflicts textually with upstream PR #25 (open, 2026-09-25), which adds a line
after the same statement. On a re-vendor, re-apply by hand: `> 1` becomes `!= 0`.

Apply (from Sources/CSignalsmithStretch), after 0001 and 0002:
    patch -p1 < patches/0003-exact-previous-hop.patch

